# Routing is now handled by prerendered static HTML: `npm run build` emits one
# real HTML file per route (dist/index.html, dist/om-oss/index.html, …) via
# scripts/prerender.mjs. Netlify serves those files directly, so the old
# per-route SPA rewrites are gone.
#
# Unknown paths (stale/old URLs) fall through to dist/404.html, which Netlify
# serves automatically with a real 404 status — so search engines drop them.
# That file is the prerendered NotFound page and hydrates into the live app.
#
# No rewrite rules are needed. When you add a new route in App.tsx, also add it
# to the seo map in src/data/site.ts (blog posts are picked up from `posts`);
# entry-server's prerenderPaths derives the build list from there.
